OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30202
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,FAs polls closed on Thursday night,
OL,8,FLabour and the Conservatives said the
OL,9,Fresult would not draw a line under the
OL,10,Fsaga.
OL,12,FSpeaking to GB News at a party-
OL,13,Forganised event in Essex, Mr Farage
OL,14,Fwas asked whether he had won, and
OL,15,Freplied: "Yeah, very convincingly,
OL,16,FI've managed to beat the establishment
OL,17,Fcandidate."
OL,26,@wD@JOUyD@KO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30203
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,FHe added: "Look, this is an
OL,8,Foverwhelming endorsement of me. I have
OL,9,Fhad enough of being judged by
OL,10,Fmainstream media, being called a
OL,11,Fcriminal.
OL,13,F"Do you know, if I made one sin, if I
OL,14,Fhaven't filled in a piece of paper,
OL,15,FI've broken no law, I've broken no tax
OL,16,Flaw, I've taken no public money, I
OL,17,Fdon't even own a motorhome.
OL,26,@oD@KOUuD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30204
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,F"Maybe I haven't filled in a piece of
OL,8,Fpaper. I'm confident that I'm right,
OL,9,Fwe'll see where we go. I put this to
OL,10,Fthe people of Clacton, said 'you
OL,11,Fdecide my future', and tonight they
OL,12,Fwill."
OL,14,FMr Farage also said he had been proved
OL,15,F"right" to call the by-election after
OL,16,Fhe claimed "attacks" and "threats"
OL,17,Ftowards his family had reduced.
OL,26,@oD@AOUtD@FO]wD@AOUwD@GO]xD@LOUxD@TO]xD@
