CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,FHe said: "You just said at the
OL,8,Fbeginning of this interview that Nigel
OL,9,FFarage is claiming victory, but in
OL,10,Fthat case it's going to be a two-
OL,11,Flegged match like the Carabao Cup or
OL,12,Fthe Cold War, because we're going to
OL,13,Fbe back again in a few weeks aren't
OL,14,Fwe? We'll see what happens then."
OL,16,FHe added: "Even if I got to 12%, so
OL,17,Fone-in-eight people in Clacton would
OL,18,Frather vote for a space warrior shaped
OL,19,Flike a bin than Nigel Farage, that
OL,20,Fwould be interesting wouldn't it?
OL,26,@oD@JOUvD@aO]xD@KOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30207
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,F"If it goes higher and higher and
OL,8,Fhigher, it says more about what the
OL,9,Factual population thinks about Nigel
OL,10,FFarage than maybe this election."
OL,12,FTurnout was 44.37%. This is just over
OL,13,F14% down on the 2024 general election
OL,14,Fturnout.
OL,16,FLabour Chair Ms Phillipson said Mr
OL,17,FFarage should "come clean with the
OL,18,Fpublic" and a Conservative Party
OL,19,Fspokesperson said the "stunt" of
OL,20,Fcalling the by-election would not draw
OL,21,Fa line under it.
OL,26,@oD@AOUrD@aO]yD@OOUzD@GO]{D@WOU{D@]O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/20
