OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,FMs Phillipson said: "Nigel Farage
OL,8,Fspent 38 days fighting a bin in his
OL,9,Fmost desperate attempt yet to deflect
OL,10,Fattention from the sleaze and scandals
OL,11,Fengulfing him and his Party.
OL,13,F"Farage may succeed in his run-off
OL,14,Fagainst a bin, but he can't run from
OL,15,Fthe truth forever. The list of
OL,16,Funanswered questions about the #5
OL,17,Fmillion gift he hid from the public,
OL,18,Fhis support from a convicted
OL,19,Ffraudster, and the mountain of other
OL,20,Fscandals he and Reform are facing
OL,21,Fisn't going away.
OL,26,@oD@UOUuD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30209
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1786681088
OL,3,CNigel Farage declares 'fairly
OL,4,Cconvincing' victory in Clacton by-
OL,5,Celection
OL,7,F"In fact, it's getting longer by the
OL,8,Fday.
OL,10,F"It's time to stop the excuses and
OL,11,Fdesperate distractions and finally
OL,12,Fcome clean with the public. If Farage
OL,13,Fhas nothing to hide, he surely would
OL,14,Fhave done so by now."
OL,16,FThe Conservative Party spokesperson
OL,17,Fsaid: "Nigel Farage called this fake
OL,18,Fby-election in a desperate attempt to
OL,19,Fdraw a line under the questions
OL,20,Fsurrounding his fishy #5 million
OL,21,Fdonation.
OL,26,@oD@AOUrD@AOUvD@UO]yD@GOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/20
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
